      "retrievedAt": "[time]",
      "excerpt": "On the origins of \"Levels\", Bergling claimed in one interview that he wanted to use a vocal sample from Etta James's \"Something's Got a Hold on Me\" and was satisfied when combining it with the hook he would use for \"Levels\". According to a 2015 Quora answer by Bergling, he first discovered the sample in the Pretty Lights song \"Finally Moving\". Bergling chose to use the sample, he said in another interview, because of the \"timeless\" and \"raw\" nature of James' vocals. Following Bergling's death, …",
